{"id": "DUYdWu0DS9K", "title": "Video by groomforwealth", "description": "Great Salespeople Don’t Fight Objections. They Solve Them.\n\nMost people think closing a fourteen-thousand-dollar deal requires pressure, persuasion, or dominance, but in reality it requires listening carefully to what is actually stopping the buyer.\n\nIn this clip, Scarlett Cardone speaks with a prospect who hesitates because she has three kids and isn’t sure how she could make it to the event, and instead of dismissing the concern she calmly reframes it.\n\nShe suggests that a babysitter could be arranged locally for the event, and if attending becomes impossible the ticket could be applied toward another event, which removes the fear of losing money.\n\nThe close doesn’t happen because of hype.\n\nIt happens because uncertainty disappears.\n\nThe moment works because it shows that high level selling is not about overpowering someone’s objection, but about reducing friction until the decision feels safe.\n\nThis isn’t really about a fourteen-thousand-dollar ticket.\n\nIt is about understanding that every objection is simply a request for reassurance, and the person who provides clarity earns the deal.\n\n#entrepreneur #success #sales #grantcardone #business", "channel": "groomforwealth", "uploader_id": "57728250213", "uploader": "CREATING WEALTH LLC", "timestamp": 1770307200, "like_count": 200426, "comment_count": 326, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1412731493122408a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 57.734, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://scontent-bog2-2.cdninstagram.com/o1/v/t2/f2